// Walkthrough findings data (generated by review/page/gen.py from the three reviewers' findings.json; do not edit by hand).
(function () { if (!window.PA) return; window.PA.REVIEW = {"lanes":[{"key":"A","label":"Building a program from nothing","short":"Building a program","intro":"One reviewer created SP-70 Precision Strike Pod in the wizard (High, carried by the F-16 Block 70), then a quick second program with no host, and tried to take the first all the way to authorization through the UI."},{"key":"B","label":"Running and assessing WS-X90","short":"Running WS-X90","intro":"Another took WS-X90 through its life cycle gates, its assessment and its authorization, and checked that each decision reached every screen that shows it."},{"key":"C","label":"Duplicated data","short":"Duplicated data","intro":"The third went through the whole menu looking for the same fact shown in several places, two pages doing one job, and whether the menu reads in the order the work is done."}],"themes":[{"key":"shell","label":"A created program is a shell","big":true,"text":"Most of its pages are empty with nothing to click, WS-X90's data shows up in it, and menu clicks switch you back to WS-X90.","ids":["A01","A02","A03","A04","A05","A06","A07","A08","A09","A10","A11","A12","A13","A14","A16","A17","A18","A19","A20","A21","A22","A23","A24","A25"]},{"key":"decisions","label":"Decisions don't respect or reach their records","big":true,"text":"Approving a gate marks its own deliverables ready, nothing checks readiness first, and Lifecycle's IATT and ATO decisions never reach Authorization.","ids":["A15","B01","B02","B06","B08","B09","B10","B11","B12","B13","B14","B29","B30","C01","C05"]},{"key":"dup","label":"The same fact on several pages","big":true,"text":"Most facts are shown on two to five pages, and after an edit some copies update and others don't.","ids":["B03","B04","B05","B17","B28","C02","C03","C04","C06","C07","C08","C09","C10","C11","C14","C15","C16","C17","C20","C21","C26","C27"]},{"key":"rmf","label":"Assessment and RMF records","text":"Determinations are per control, results are published on a draft plan, and there's no place for the SCA's recommendation or the AO's decision type.","ids":["B16","B18","B19","B20","B21","B22","B23","B27"]},{"key":"order","label":"Order of the work","text":"The menu groups pages by kind of record, and some steps are scheduled out of order.","ids":["B15","B24","C24","C25"]},{"key":"wiring","label":"Not wired, wrong names","text":"Verbs that answer \"Not saved\", another program's names, and people missing from People.","ids":["B07","B25","B26","C12","C13","C18","C19","C22","C23","C28"]}],"findings":[{"id":"A03","lane":"A","sev":"blocker","kind":"flow","theme":"shell","what":"With a created program current, any program-menu link followed from Lifecycle, Boundary, Host & providers, the SCTM workbook or a record page makes WS-X90 current: the page and switcher turn to WS-X90. Close the workbook lands on WS-X90's Overview.","why":"The user is dropped into WS-X90's data mid-task, unnoticed; every later step and edit lands on the wrong program.","fix":"Add lifecycle, boundary, hosts, sctm and rec--* to the hubs layer's program pages (PROG_PAGES); only the switcher, or a link naming a program, changes the current program.","evidence":"SP-70 current: Lifecycle → ITCSC gave 'WS-X90 › ITCSC', cur=PRG-1090; Lifecycle → Overview, Boundary → Controls (560), Host & providers → Overview, PE-3 page → Composition all opened WS-X90's.","where":"#lifecycle, #boundary, #hosts, #sctm, rec--* record pages → any program-menu link","links":[{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle","label":"Lifecycle"},{"t":"route","r":"boundary","label":"Boundary"},{"t":"route","r":"hosts","label":"Host & providers"},{"t":"route","r":"sctm","label":"SCTM workbook"}],"same":[],"lead":{"verdict":"held","note":"With SP-70 current, Lifecycle, then ITCSC in the program menu, opened \"WS-X90 › ITCSC\"."}},{"id":"A04","lane":"A","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"shell","what":"The created program's SCTM workbook is WS-X90's: 'WS-X90 · SCTM workbook · Snapshot Nov 17, 2026 · SSP revision 3 draft', WS-X90's controls and filters, while the switcher reads PRG-2301.","why":"The user stages edits to another program's traceability matrix believing it is theirs.","fix":"Draw the workbook from the current program (its 555 controls, its requirements, draft SSP revision 1), or an empty state naming SP-70.","evidence":"Switcher PRG-2301 → Compliance › SCTM workbook: 'WS-X90 ¦ SCTM workbook ¦ Snapshot Nov 17, 2026 ¦ SSP revision 3 draft'.","where":"#sctm (SP-70 current)","links":[{"t":"route","r":"sctm","label":"SCTM workbook"}],"same":[],"lead":{"verdict":"held","note":"With SP-70 current, the SCTM workbook reads \"WS-X90 SCTM workbook · Snapshot Nov 17, 2026 · SSP revision 3 draft\"."}},{"id":"A05","lane":"A","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"shell","what":"SP-70's hybrid controls show WS-X90's part; PE-3 reads Satisfied, 12/12 mapped, evidenced and assessed, 'Implementation in SSP 3 … SYS-WSX90', beside Requirements 0, Assessment 0. F-16's preview says 'What WS-X90 takes'.","why":"A new program shows satisfied, assessed controls it never touched; an SCA or AO would read WS-X90's results as SP-70's.","fix":"A created program's controls read its own standing (No requirement) and an empty part to write; only the provider's part and status come from the host.","evidence":"Its part (PE-3, PE-14, MA-2, SC-7): 'WS-X90 seals its LRU access panels…'; PE-3 preview: 'No requirement maps PE-3 yet', 'No assessment has judged PE-3 yet'; record: 'Next step: None: an assessor found it satisfied'.","where":"#hosts, preview: a-tests-control PE-3, rec--a-tests-control--PE-3, preview: v2h-prov f16","links":[{"t":"route","r":"rec--a-tests-control--PE-3","label":"PE-3 control page"},{"t":"panel","k":"a-tests-control","id":"PE-3","label":"Control preview: PE-3 Physical Access Control"},{"t":"panel","k":"v2h-prov","id":"f16","label":"Host system preview: F-16 Block 70"},{"t":"route","r":"hosts","label":"Host & providers"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A06","lane":"A","sev":"blocker","kind":"dead-end","theme":"shell","what":"Every build page of a created program reads 'Nothing recorded for PRG-2301 yet · … fills in as SP-70 records its work' with no action: no Create element, Add interconnection, Add port, Tailor control or Create policy.","why":"Build steps (composition, inventory, interconnections, ports, baseline, policies) cannot be done, and nothing says where else to do them.","fix":"Give each page its first action (Create element, Add interconnection, Add port, Tailor a control, Upload policy) over what the wizard already wrote.","evidence":"Swept all program-menu pages from Overview with SP-70 current, then PRG-2302: same empty state, UI lists no control on these pages.","where":"#composition, #inventory, #stigs, #interconnections, #ppsm, #baseline, #policies, #checks (created program)","links":[{"t":"route","r":"composition","label":"Composition"},{"t":"route","r":"inventory","label":"Inventory"},{"t":"route","r":"stigs","label":"STIG checklists"},{"t":"route","r":"interconnections","label":"Interconnections"},{"t":"route","r":"ppsm","label":"Ports & protocols"},{"t":"route","r":"baseline","label":"Baseline"},{"t":"route","r":"policies","label":"Policies"},{"t":"route","r":"checks","label":"Checks"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A11","lane":"A","sev":"blocker","kind":"dead-end","theme":"shell","what":"The chain cannot start: no Create requirement, no evidence path for the new system, the SSP page loops back to the starter guide, assessment waits for an SSP nothing can publish; Findings, POA&M, Risks, Authorization have no create action.","why":"Requirement → mapping → evidence → narrative → assessment → finding → POA&M → package is impossible for any new program.","fix":"Create requirement and Map control on Requirements, Upload evidence, an SSP editor with Publish, Plan assessment, Create finding/risk/POA&M item, Start package; break the guide/page loops.","evidence":"More requirement actions: only 'Open the SCTM workbook'; Add source's System step lacks SYS-2301; SSP: 'the starter guide's Draft the SSP step opens it'; Plan delta: 'waits for a published SSP'.","where":"#requirements, #evidence, #ssp, #assessments, #findings, #poam, #risks, #authorization (created program)","links":[{"t":"route","r":"requirements","label":"Requirements"},{"t":"route","r":"evidence","label":"Evidence"},{"t":"route","r":"ssp","label":"SSP"},{"t":"route","r":"assessments","label":"Assessments"},{"t":"route","r":"findings","label":"Findings"},{"t":"route","r":"poam","label":"POA&M"},{"t":"route","r":"risks","label":"Risks"},{"t":"route","r":"authorization","label":"Authorization"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A10","lane":"A","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"shell","what":"The starter guide's progress is one list shared by every created program: creating PRG-2302 reset SP-70 from 6 to 2 of 10, and a step ticked on SP-70 shows done on PRG-2302.","why":"Progress is lost when a second program is created, and one program reports another's work as done.","fix":"Keep the guide's state per program (prog.guide keyed by program code), seeded from each program's own facts.","evidence":"state.prog.guide = ['baseline','roles','sources'] for both; SP-70 6 of 10 before PRG-2302, 2 of 10 after; ticked Connect evidence sources on SP-70 → PRG-2302 'done, mark as not done'.","where":"#program-start, #getting-started (both created programs)","links":[{"t":"route","r":"program-start","label":"Start page"},{"t":"route","r":"getting-started","label":"Getting started"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A08","lane":"A","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"shell","what":"Lifecycle dates contradict the wizard: target authorization Sep 30, 2027 (guide: submit by Aug 31, 2027) but Lifecycle's ATO is due May 30, 2030 and Select security controls Oct 23, 2027, after the target.","why":"The PM and ISSM get two schedules for one program; the dates they entered are ignored by the life cycle.","fix":"Date the lifecycle template back from the wizard's target authorization date, or ask for milestone dates in the wizard.","evidence":"Wizard: start Dec 1, 2026, target Sep 30, 2027. Lifecycle: Categorize Mar 7, 2027; Select Oct 23, 2027; IATT Jun 4, 2029; ATO May 30, 2030 ('archive's 19-step template').","where":"#lifecycle vs #program-start","links":[{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle","label":"Lifecycle"},{"t":"route","r":"program-start","label":"Start page"}],"same":[],"lead":{"verdict":"held","note":"Lifecycle's ATO step is due May 30, 2030; the wizard's target authorization was Sep 30, 2027."}},{"id":"A01","lane":"A","sev":"major","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"shell","what":"Blank program still prefills the product example: name 'Customer D · X800 Eject Launch Integration', X800's mission, system 'Customer D mission system', element code prefix 'CD-'; library elements coded CD-CM and CD-KLI.","why":"A user who skims creates a program named for another customer, with codes that match nothing of theirs.","fix":"Blank program starts empty (placeholders only); element codes derive from the system code typed (SYS-2301 → SP70-).","evidence":"Start: Blank program → pn-name='Customer D · X800 Eject Launch Integration'; pn-s0-name='Customer D mission system'; pn-ae-code='CD-'; Add from library gave CD-CM, CD-KLI.","where":"#program-new-details, #program-new-systems","links":[{"t":"route","r":"program-new-details","label":"Create program · Program"},{"t":"route","r":"program-new-systems","label":"Create program · Systems"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A02","lane":"A","sev":"major","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"shell","what":"Program tailoring arrives pre-applied with Customer D's decisions, on a blank strike pod and on the quick path: remove PE-17 ('maintained only at Customer D's depot'), add SR-4 ('the ejector's components').","why":"Another customer's tailoring and rationale are recorded on this program's profile unless the user notices and deletes them.","fix":"No tailoring by default; offer suggestions with an explicit Add, never pre-applied.","evidence":"Baseline step: 'Removes PE-17 … Customer D's depot', 'Adds SR-4 … ejector's components', stack 'Program tailoring +1 −1' before any edit; second program kept them (Tailoring +1 −1).","where":"#program-new-baseline, dialog: pn-tailor","links":[{"t":"dialog","label":"Tailor for this program"},{"t":"route","r":"program-new-baseline","label":"Create program · Baseline"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A07","lane":"A","sev":"major","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"shell","what":"What the wizard wrote is not shown where it lives: Composition and Baseline read 'Nothing recorded'; Controls 'No control is mapped yet' links to the empty Baseline; Boundary omits the 4 elements; People lists no role.","why":"Header facts (Systems 1 · Elements 4 · Controls 555 · Roles 6 of 6) contradict the pages that should hold them.","fix":"Composition lists SYS-2301 and its elements; Baseline shows the stack (the guide's View panel already has it); Controls lists 555 at No requirement; People lists the roles.","evidence":"Start page facts Systems 1, Elements 4, Controls 555; guide's baseline View panel shows the 4-layer stack; Baseline page 'Nothing recorded for PRG-2301 yet'; Boundary 'What it covers 2'.","where":"#composition, #baseline, #controls, #boundary, #people (SP-70)","links":[{"t":"route","r":"composition","label":"Composition"},{"t":"route","r":"baseline","label":"Baseline"},{"t":"route","r":"controls","label":"Controls"},{"t":"route","r":"boundary","label":"Boundary"},{"t":"route","r":"people","label":"People"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A09","lane":"A","sev":"major","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"shell","what":"Lifecycle's RMF steps 'Categorize the system' and 'Select security controls' stay Not started, though the wizard categorized H/H/H with a rationale, chose a 555-control baseline the guide marks done, and the ITCSC was 'signed'.","why":"Decisions made in the wizard and guide never reach the life cycle; the user cannot tell what is left.","fix":"Mark Categorize and Select done, or 'awaiting signature', with the wizard's values and date.","evidence":"Guide: 'Choose the control baseline' and 'Sign the ITCSC' done; Lifecycle: 'Categorize the system, Not started' (Not ready: ITCSC), 'Select security controls, Not started'.","where":"#lifecycle","links":[{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle","label":"Lifecycle"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A12","lane":"A","sev":"major","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"shell","what":"Getting started measures clicks, not work: three file drops tick their steps importing nothing, and any step is ticked by hand; SP-70 reached 60% with no requirement, empty ITCSC, no mapping.","why":"The percentage in the menu and on Home misleads the PM and AO about readiness.","fix":"Derive each step from the record it names (requirements imported, ITCSC signed, mappings); a file drop shows what it read, or says it is not wired.","evidence":"Import requirements → guide 3 of 10, Requirements 'No requirements yet'; diagram drop → 5 of 10, shown nowhere; ticked Map requirements → 6 of 10, Controls 'No control is mapped yet'.","where":"#program-start, dialogs: pn-reqs, pn-itcsc, pn-diagram","links":[{"t":"dialog","label":"Import requirements"},{"t":"dialog","label":"Import the ITCSC"},{"t":"dialog","label":"Upload the architecture diagram"},{"t":"route","r":"program-start","label":"Start page"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A13","lane":"A","sev":"major","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"shell","what":"Host inheritance is ignored outside the host pages: the start page says 'What the program inherits: Nothing', and Programs and Home show 0 of 555, though F-16 gives 12 inherited controls reading Satisfied.","why":"WS-X90's 227 counts its 52 inherited controls; a new program counts none, so the same rule gives two answers.","fix":"The inherits card lists the host's 12 inherited and 4 hybrid; satisfied counts include inherited controls by the provider's status, as WS-X90's does.","evidence":"Start page: 'Nothing: the program does not start from a product'; Programs row '0 of 555'; Host & providers: 12 Inherited, provider's status Satisfied.","where":"#program-start, #portfolio, #home vs #hosts","links":[{"t":"route","r":"program-start","label":"Start page"},{"t":"route","r":"portfolio","label":"Programs"},{"t":"route","r":"home","label":"Home"},{"t":"route","r":"hosts","label":"Host & providers"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A14","lane":"A","sev":"major","kind":"missing","theme":"shell","what":"The created program's ITCSC is an empty page with no action, though the wizard captured categorization, information types, rationale, NSS overlay and team; 'Sign the ITCSC' is marked done by dropping a file, nobody signing.","why":"The categorization record an AF program must sign is blank, while the guide says it is signed.","fix":"Create the ITCSC draft from the wizard (§10, §6, §7, §11 filled), with Sign for the PM and AO; done only once both signed.","evidence":"ITCSC: 'Nothing recorded for PRG-2301 yet · ITCSC fills in as SP-70 records its work', no button; after Import: 'Sign the ITCSC: done', ITCSC unchanged.","where":"#itcsc (created program), dialog: pn-itcsc","links":[{"t":"dialog","label":"Import the ITCSC"},{"t":"route","r":"itcsc","label":"ITCSC"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A15","lane":"A","sev":"major","kind":"flow","theme":"decisions","what":"Approve is accepted with 0 of 1 deliverables and 0 of 3 criteria met, and recording it rewrites the gate to '1 of 1 ready' and '3 of 3 met'. The decider is 'Chief engineer', no person named.","why":"A gate decision fabricates readiness evidence; anyone can record for an unnamed role.","fix":"Keep deliverables and criteria as they were; ask for conditions when unmet; name the decider when requesting; only that person records.","evidence":"Record decision header: '0 of 1 deliverables ready · 0 of 3 criteria met'; Approve → preview 'Deliverables 1 of 1 ready', 'Criteria 3 of 3 met', 'Recorded by Ingrid Solberg'.","where":"#review-queue, preview: a-work-gate asr-1, dialog: v2g-decide","links":[{"t":"panel","k":"a-work-gate","id":"asr-1","label":"Lifecycle gate preview: ASR · Alternative systems review"},{"t":"dialog","label":"Record decision"},{"t":"route","r":"review-queue","label":"Review queue"}],"same":["B02","C01"],"lead":null},{"id":"A16","lane":"A","sev":"major","kind":"flow","theme":"shell","what":"Switching from one created program to another keeps the address at #program-start, so the previous program's page stays drawn and the switcher shows its name above the new program's stage line.","why":"The user believes they switched, then reads and ticks the other program's guide.","fix":"Redraw on switch even when the route is unchanged (V2.redraw after setCur), and draw the switcher from the current program.","evidence":"PRG-2302 → SP-70: cur=PRG-2301, main 'Customer D · X800 Eject Launch Integration', switcher 'PRG-2302 … next Milestone A Jan 31, 2027' (SP-70's stage).","where":"switcher between two created programs (#program-start)","links":[{"t":"route","r":"program-start","label":"Start page"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A17","lane":"A","sev":"major","kind":"missing","theme":"shell","what":"The starter guide assigns each step an owner and due date, but none reaches My work: 'Draft the SSP', assigned to me, due Jan 15, 2027, is absent.","why":"Owners never learn they owe a step; the guide is the only place it lives.","fix":"Each guide step with an owner becomes a task in that person's My work, linked back to the step.","evidence":"Guide: Draft the SSP · Ingrid Solberg · Due Jan 15, 2027; My work (Ingrid): only WS-X90 items, badge 13 unchanged.","where":"#program-start vs #my-work","links":[{"t":"route","r":"program-start","label":"Start page"},{"t":"route","r":"my-work","label":"My work"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A18","lane":"A","sev":"minor","kind":"wording","theme":"shell","what":"A blank program's pages name Customer D and a product it lacks: 'Customer D's requirements', 'the product's evidence', 'Assist can draft from the product's narratives', invite placeholder name@customer-d.mil; footnote cites X800 Missile's claims.","why":"The user is told to import another customer's document and expect product narratives that do not exist.","fix":"Word each step from the program: 'the customer's requirements', 'ACAS scans and STIG checklists'; drop product phrases when no product.","evidence":"SP-70 starter guide and Import requirements dialog text; Invite by email placeholder 'name@customer-d.mil'.","where":"#program-start, #sources, dialogs: pn-reqs, pn-invite","links":[{"t":"dialog","label":"Import requirements"},{"t":"dialog","label":"Invite by email"},{"t":"route","r":"program-start","label":"Start page"},{"t":"route","r":"sources","label":"Evidence sources"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A19","lane":"A","sev":"minor","kind":"duplication","theme":"shell","what":"For a created program, Overview and Getting started draw the same starter-guide page as #program-start; there is no overview of control status or the life cycle.","why":"Two menu entries open one page; the user looks for an overview that never appears.","fix":"Keep one entry (Getting started) until the program has data, or give Overview the control status band at 0.","evidence":"Program menu Overview → starter guide; Getting started → identical text.","where":"#overview, #getting-started, #program-start (created program)","links":[{"t":"route","r":"overview","label":"Overview"},{"t":"route","r":"getting-started","label":"Getting started"},{"t":"route","r":"program-start","label":"Start page"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A20","lane":"A","sev":"minor","kind":"flow","theme":"shell","what":"The wizard never asks whether the system is an NSS (ITCSC §7); the quick product path lands a weapon variant on High (370) without CNSSI 1253, which is only recommended, and preselects F-16 as host.","why":"A hurried user creates a DoD weapon program on the wrong baseline.","fix":"Ask the NSS question in Systems and apply CNSSI 1253 when yes; never preselect a host.","evidence":"Second program with defaults: Review 'High baseline · No overlays · 370 controls'; Systems step arrived with 'F-16 Block 70' checked.","where":"#program-new-systems, #program-new-baseline (quick path)","links":[{"t":"route","r":"program-new-systems","label":"Create program · Systems"},{"t":"route","r":"program-new-baseline","label":"Create program · Baseline"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A21","lane":"A","sev":"minor","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"shell","what":"A third draft proposes system code SYS-2301, already SP-70's system, and accepts it, while the program code advanced to PRG-2303 and is 'checked against every program's code'.","why":"Two systems share one code, breaking the references that use it.","fix":"Propose the next free system code and check it as the program code is checked.","evidence":"Blank draft after SP-70 existed: pn-s0-code='SYS-2301'; Continue moved to Baseline with no error; pn-code='PRG-2303'.","where":"#program-new-systems","links":[{"t":"route","r":"program-new-systems","label":"Create program · Systems"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A22","lane":"A","sev":"minor","kind":"missing","theme":"shell","what":"Search finds neither created program by name or code.","why":"A user returning later cannot find the program they made except through Programs or the switcher.","fix":"Index created programs (name, code, system code) in search.","evidence":"'SP-70', 'Strike Pod', 'PRG-2301' → 'No results'; 'WS-X90' finds its campaigns.","where":"search (⌘K)","links":[{"t":"text","label":"Search (⌘K)"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A23","lane":"A","sev":"minor","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"shell","what":"SP-70's Programs row shows Owner '—' and raises No owner from 4 to 5, though the wizard named Marcus Ryde system owner; the row opens the program while other rows open a preview.","why":"The owner chosen in the wizard is lost on the register; the filter counts it wrong.","fix":"Owner reads the system owner from step 3; the row opens the program preview like the others.","evidence":"Programs: SP-70 row '—'; 'No owner 5' (was 4); tr data-go='program-start' without data-panel.","where":"#portfolio","links":[{"t":"route","r":"portfolio","label":"Programs"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A24","lane":"A","sev":"minor","kind":"dead-end","theme":"shell","what":"Host & providers says 'Add a provider when one offers controls' but offers no Add provider action (WS-X90's page has one).","why":"A program that later gains a host or common control provider cannot record it.","fix":"Show Add provider on a created program's page.","evidence":"PRG-2302 Host & providers: 'No host system … Add a provider when one offers controls.'; UI lists no control.","where":"#hosts (program with no host)","links":[{"t":"route","r":"hosts","label":"Host & providers"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"A25","lane":"A","sev":"minor","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"shell","what":"The inherits card says Inherited 175 and, beneath, that configuration B satisfies 170 of 370 High controls.","why":"More controls inherited than the product satisfies reads as an error to an assessor.","fix":"State the rule (inherited = satisfied or claimed and judged?) or make the numbers agree.","evidence":"'Inherited 175 · Shared 59 · To assess 136 … configuration B satisfies 170 of 370 High controls'.","where":"#program-start (PRG-2302)","links":[{"t":"route","r":"program-start","label":"Start page"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B01","lane":"B","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"decisions","what":"PDR deliverable Interconnections reads Ready, 'Agreements current', while the Interconnections page it opens shows 2 expired MOUs, 2 unsigned draft ISAs (SIPRNet, telemetry) and 2 expiring within 90 days.","why":"The chief engineer approves PDR on a readiness the source record contradicts.","fix":"Read the deliverable from Interconnections: Not ready, '2 expired · 2 unsigned', and open the page on those views.","evidence":"lifecycle-pdr-2 → 'Ready: Interconnections' → #interconnections: All 9, Expiring in 90 days 2, No agreement 2, Expired 2 (Mission data loads MOU expired Oct 31, Depot maintenance laptop MOU expired Sep 30).","where":"lifecycle-pdr-2","links":[{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-pdr-2","label":"Lifecycle › PDR · Preliminary design review · Increment 2"}],"same":[],"lead":{"verdict":"held","note":"PDR lists \"Interconnections · Ready · Agreements current\"; the Interconnections page counts 2 expired and 2 with no agreement."}},{"id":"B02","lane":"B","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"decisions","what":"Recording a decision rewrites its inputs: deliverables flip to Ready (Requirements 'Traced', Boundary 'Reviewed by the SCA', memo 'Signed', SAR step 'Assessment campaign Completed · SAR Published') and Approve sets criteria met; the records stay unchanged.","why":"Gates claim traced, signed, assessed; Overview, Controls and Assessments say otherwise. Two truths.","fix":"A decision records only the decision. Deliverables and criteria keep reading their records; with conditions, unmet items stay open.","evidence":"PDR approved with conditions → 5 of 5 ready; Overview still 'No requirement 14'. Inc 2 SAR approved → 'Assessment campaign · Completed'; #assessments has no Increment 2 campaign.","where":"lifecycle-pdr-2, lifecycle-strat-2, lifecycle-iatt-2, lifecycle-sar-2, dialog: v2g-decide","links":[{"t":"dialog","label":"Record decision"},{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-pdr-2","label":"Lifecycle › PDR · Preliminary design review · Increment 2"},{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-strat-2","label":"Lifecycle › AO approval of the RMF strategy · Increment 2"},{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-iatt-2","label":"Lifecycle › IATT · Interim authority to test · Increment 2"},{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-sar-2","label":"Lifecycle › Final assessment and SAR · Increment 2"}],"same":["A15","C01"],"lead":null},{"id":"B03","lane":"B","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"dup","what":"Baseline's status key does not move after results are published: it stays Satisfied 227, Other than satisfied 13, Not assessed 86 while Overview and Controls show 240 / 14 / 68.","why":"The page that shapes the baseline shows a standing that contradicts Overview and Controls.","fix":"Read Baseline's key from the same control-status source as Overview and Controls.","evidence":"Published FY2027 results (AC-2(7) OTS) and the expanded interim results: Overview 41%→43%, Satisfied 227→240, OTS 13→14, Not assessed 86→68; #baseline key unchanged.","where":"baseline","links":[{"t":"route","r":"baseline","label":"Baseline"}],"same":["C07"],"lead":{"verdict":"held","note":"Publishing the interim results moved Overview and Controls from 227 to 240 satisfied; Baseline, Posture and Findings drew exactly what they drew before."}},{"id":"B04","lane":"B","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"dup","what":"Posture's band keeps Open issues 44 and Open risks 40 after a publication opens an issue and a risk is created; Findings, Overview and Risks show 45 and 41.","why":"The analysis view undercounts what is open; numbers disagree across screens.","fix":"Count Posture's issues and risks from the live registers.","evidence":"Publish FY2027 results → issue opened (Findings 44→45, High 12→13); Create risk → Risks 40→41. #posture: 'Open issues 44 · Open risks 40'.","where":"posture","links":[{"t":"route","r":"posture","label":"Posture"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B05","lane":"B","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"dup","what":"After the assessment chain, the ATO condition still reads '12 high issues open' (Findings: 13 High), Continuous monitoring's trigger says the same, and Package room still says 'POA&M current: 41 items' while Authorization says 42.","why":"The AO's conditions and the package show stale progress.","fix":"Derive condition progress and package counts from Findings and POA&M at draw time.","evidence":"New High issue on AC-2(7) and its POA&M item → Authorization 'POA&M 42 items'; condition '12 high issues open · Dec 17'; package-room Versions 'POA&M current: 41 items'.","where":"authorization, package-room, conmon","links":[{"t":"route","r":"authorization","label":"Authorization"},{"t":"route","r":"package-room","label":"Package room"},{"t":"route","r":"conmon","label":"Continuous monitoring"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B06","lane":"B","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"decisions","what":"Authorization's decision history dates Increment 1's IATT Jun 2, 2026 (ATD Aug 31, 2026, 'Developmental test article'); Lifecycle's IATT step says decided and memo signed Nov 18, 2025.","why":"Two dates for one authorization; an auditor cannot tell which IATT covered flight test.","fix":"One IATT record read by both pages, with its test configuration and expiry.","evidence":"#authorization Decision history: 'IATT · Developmental test article · Jun 2, 2026 · Aug 31, 2026'. #lifecycle-iatt-1: 'IATT memo · Signed Nov 18, 2025'.","where":"authorization, lifecycle-iatt-1","links":[{"t":"route","r":"authorization","label":"Authorization"},{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-iatt-1","label":"Lifecycle › IATT · Interim authority to test · Increment 1"}],"same":["C05"],"lead":{"verdict":"held","note":"Authorization's Package tab lists \"IATT · Developmental test article · Jun 2, 2026\"; Lifecycle's IATT step says the memo was signed Nov 18, 2025."}},{"id":"B07","lane":"B","sev":"blocker","kind":"dead-end","theme":"wiring","what":"SSP 3's review page 'Submit for review' does nothing once readiness has no blocker; SSP stays 'Not submitted'. Package version 2 waits on 'SSP 3 approved', so no authorization decision can be requested or recorded.","why":"The authorization path ends; the AO's decision is unreachable.","fix":"Make Submit for review send SSP 3 to its approvers and let their approval satisfy the package gate.","evidence":"Accepted the AI categorization rationale → 'Readiness 6 warnings' → Submit for review: no dialog, no toast; #ssps panel 'Approval Not submitted'; Submit for approval still 'SSP 3 approved · Draft'.","where":"ssp-review → authorization, dialog: v7p-submit","links":[{"t":"dialog","label":"Submit package version 2 for approval"},{"t":"route","r":"ssp-review","label":"SSP 3 · Submit for review"},{"t":"route","r":"authorization","label":"Authorization"}],"same":[],"lead":{"verdict":"refuted","note":"Submit for review first asks for a review comment (\"Write a review comment for the ISSM before you submit\"). With one, it says the categorization has no rationale and offers \"Submit anyway as a draft for ISSM review\". It works; the reviewer missed the comment field."}},{"id":"B08","lane":"B","sev":"blocker","kind":"flow","theme":"decisions","what":"Order is a chain, not a gate: on Nov 17, 2026 the user requests and approves Strategy, MS-B, SSP, CDR, TRR, IATT, SVR, SAR, ATO and IOC (due 2027), each at 0 deliverables ready. Approve reads 'Every criterion is met'.","why":"An ATO and an IATT are recorded with no assessment, no test configuration, a year early.","fix":"Block Approve while deliverables or criteria are open (allow with conditions or Not approved); warn on request; refuse decisions far before due.","evidence":"Each dialog: '0 of N deliverables ready · 0 of N criteria met' → toast '… approved'. Lifecycle: 'Increment 2 · Ops · every step done'.","where":"lifecycle (Increment 2), dialog: v2g-request, v2g-decide","links":[{"t":"dialog","label":"Request decision"},{"t":"dialog","label":"Record decision"},{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle","label":"Lifecycle"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B09","lane":"B","sev":"major","kind":"missing","theme":"decisions","what":"Lifecycle's IATT and ATO decisions never reach Authorization, Boundary or Package room: after approving Increment 2's IATT and ATO, Authorization still shows only Increment 1's ATO; Boundary still 'IATT planned May 18, 2027'. Authorization never lists Increment 2's IATT.","why":"The authorization record and the life cycle disagree on what is authorized.","fix":"One authorization record per decision, written by the ATO and IATT steps and read by Authorization, Boundary and Package room.","evidence":"z11 walk: Authorization, Boundary, Assessments, Package room texts identical before and after; Overview header still 'ATO with conditions' (Increment 1).","where":"authorization, boundary, package-room","links":[{"t":"route","r":"authorization","label":"Authorization"},{"t":"route","r":"boundary","label":"Boundary"},{"t":"route","r":"package-room","label":"Package room"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B10","lane":"B","sev":"major","kind":"missing","theme":"decisions","what":"'Approve with conditions' promises 'conditions are tracked to a day', but conditions show only on the step page: Lifecycle rows read Passed or Completed (Increment 1's ATO too), My work drops both open PDR items, nothing carries the due day.","why":"Nobody is reminded of the conditions a gate passed on; they vanish.","fix":"Show 'Passed with conditions' on the row and create a tracked condition (owner, due day) on My work and Lifecycle until closed.","evidence":"PDR approved with conditions ('… by Jan 15, 2027'): no 'Jan 15'/'condition' on Lifecycle, My work, Schedule, Overview. #lifecycle ATO-1 row 'Completed'.","where":"lifecycle, my-work, schedule","links":[{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle","label":"Lifecycle"},{"t":"route","r":"my-work","label":"My work"},{"t":"route","r":"schedule","label":"Schedule"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B11","lane":"B","sev":"major","kind":"flow","theme":"decisions","what":"Multi-step gate approvals collapse: one Record decision (by Ingrid, a security engineer) marks the ISSM's step 1 and the AO's step 2 both Approved; the dialog names only the AO. Risk acceptance does walk its three steps.","why":"The approval chain the request set up is never walked; the ISSM never decides.","fix":"Record one step at a time, as risk acceptance does: the dialog names the current holder; the next step is asked after it.","evidence":"Request: 'Joel Barrantes is asked first'. Record: 'Decided by R. Calloway'. One submit → STEP 1 and STEP 2 'Approved Nov 17', 'Recorded by Ingrid Solberg'.","where":"lifecycle-strat-2, dialog: v2g-decide","links":[{"t":"dialog","label":"Record decision"},{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-strat-2","label":"Lifecycle › AO approval of the RMF strategy · Increment 2"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B12","lane":"B","sev":"major","kind":"dead-end","theme":"decisions","what":"PDR deliverable 'Boundary · Not ready · SCA review pending' opens Boundary on Increment 1 as fielded (ATO/IATT toggle). No Block 1.1 design boundary and no SCA review appear anywhere.","why":"The reviewer cannot see what is pending or act on it.","fix":"Open Boundary on Increment 2 · Block 1.1 with the SCA's boundary review shown and requestable.","evidence":"#boundary: 'Increment 1 · Block 1, the six subsystems as fielded'; no 'SCA' or 'review' text.","where":"lifecycle-pdr-2 → boundary","links":[{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-pdr-2","label":"Lifecycle › PDR · Preliminary design review · Increment 2"},{"t":"route","r":"boundary","label":"Boundary"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B13","lane":"B","sev":"major","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"decisions","what":"After the RMF strategy is approved its gate shows RM.3 met, while Security engineering and the Milestone B gate still show RM.3 'Not assessed'. Security engineering lists no RMF strategy step. (PDR's criteria and outcomes do agree.)","why":"The same outcome is met and not assessed on the same day.","fix":"One status per outcome per increment, read by every gate and by Security engineering.","evidence":"Strat approved → Criteria 2 of 2 met (RM.3). #sse 'RM.3 … Not assessed No evidence'; #lifecycle-ms-b-2 Criteria 0 of 4.","where":"sse, lifecycle-strat-2, lifecycle-ms-b-2","links":[{"t":"route","r":"sse","label":"Security engineering"},{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-strat-2","label":"Lifecycle › AO approval of the RMF strategy · Increment 2"},{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-ms-b-2","label":"Lifecycle › Milestone B decision · Increment 2"}],"same":["C01"],"lead":null},{"id":"B14","lane":"B","sev":"major","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"decisions","what":"Increment 2's 'Develop the SSP' reads Not started while its own deliverable, SSP revision 3, is a Draft started Nov 13 (Overview, SCTM header, CDR deliverable, My work 'Submit SSP 3 for review').","why":"SSP work under way is invisible on the life cycle.","fix":"Derive the step's status from SSP 3: In progress, Draft, 74 placeholder narratives.","evidence":"#lifecycle-ssp-2: 'Not started', 'SSP revision 3 · Draft'. #overview: 'Revision 3 · Draft · 74 placeholder narratives · started Nov 13'.","where":"lifecycle-ssp-2, overview","links":[{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-ssp-2","label":"Lifecycle › Develop the SSP · Increment 2"},{"t":"route","r":"overview","label":"Overview"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B15","lane":"B","sev":"major","kind":"flow","theme":"order","what":"Increment 1's FY2027 annual update (package version 2) waits on SSP 3, which drafts Block 1.1: Lifecycle makes it Increment 2's CDR deliverable and ConMon flags it a significant change. Increment 2's CVI can only use SSP 2.","why":"Increment 2's design rides into Increment 1's annual update before PDR closes.","fix":"Separate revisions: Increment 1's annual SSP update, and Increment 2's SSP feeding its own IATT and ATO.","evidence":"Package room Versions: 'FY2027 annual update: SSP 3 with the Block 1.1 configuration'. ConMon trigger 'SSP 3 drafts the Block 1.1 configuration · Review'. CVI 'Plan an assessment': only 'SSP 2, published Jul 25'.","where":"authorization, package-room, ssp, conmon","links":[{"t":"route","r":"authorization","label":"Authorization"},{"t":"route","r":"package-room","label":"Package room"},{"t":"route","r":"ssp","label":"SSP"},{"t":"route","r":"conmon","label":"Continuous monitoring"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B16","lane":"B","sev":"major","kind":"wording","theme":"rmf","what":"Result batches are named 'expanded control set, increment 1/2', colliding with acquisition Increments: 'Increment 2 results published' gates Increment 1's package; publishing toasts 'Increment 2 published'.","why":"An AO reads Block 1.1 as assessed while it is at PDR.","fix":"Name result batches 'set 1', 'set 2' or by date; keep 'Increment' for acquisition increments.","evidence":"Review queue 'Interim results — expanded control set, increment 2'; submit dialog 'Increment 2 results published'; toast 'Increment 2 published: 20 determinations…'. ATO-1 conditions concern Increment 1.","where":"assessments, review-queue, authorization, dialog: v7p-submit","links":[{"t":"dialog","label":"Submit package version 2 for approval"},{"t":"route","r":"assessments","label":"Assessments"},{"t":"route","r":"review-queue","label":"Review queue"},{"t":"route","r":"authorization","label":"Authorization"}],"same":[],"lead":{"verdict":"held","note":"Publishing the expanded results toasts \"Increment 2 published: 20 determinations now decide WS-X90's control statuses\", and package version 2's checklist reads \"Increment 2 results published\"."}},{"id":"B17","lane":"B","sev":"major","kind":"duplication","theme":"dup","what":"AC-2(7)'s page says Campaign — and offers 'Add to assessment campaign', while the Expanded campaign holds a Ready evidence request for AC-2(7). Following the step adds it to a second campaign.","why":"One control is assessed twice; the control page hides the first campaign.","fix":"Read a control's campaign from every campaign's requests and plans; offer 'Open assessment campaign' when one holds it.","evidence":"#campaign Requests: 'Privileged role table and membership change log export, LRU-013 · AC-2(7) · Ready'. Control page: 'Campaign —', next step 'Add to assessment campaign'.","where":"rec--a-tests-control--AC-2(7), campaign","links":[{"t":"route","r":"rec--a-tests-control--AC-2(7)","label":"AC-2(7) control page"},{"t":"route","r":"campaign","label":"Expanded Control Set Assessment"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B18","lane":"B","sev":"major","kind":"missing","theme":"rmf","what":"No assessment objectives or test procedures to work: Objectives lists controls with counts; Record determination takes one value per control; afterwards the control reads 'Assessed 4 of 4 objectives'. No examine, interview or test methods anywhere.","why":"An SCA cannot record SP 800-53A determinations per objective with method and evidence.","fix":"List each objective with its methods; record a determination per objective; derive the control's status from them.","evidence":"Objectives tab: 'AC-2(7) Privileged User Accounts 4 · Added Nov 17'. Dialog: Satisfied / Partially / Other than satisfied + Rationale. Registry search: no screen shows Examine, Interview or test procedure.","where":"campaign-conmon, dialog: Record determination","links":[{"t":"dialog","label":"Record determination"},{"t":"route","r":"campaign-conmon","label":"Continuous monitoring FY2027 campaign"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B19","lane":"B","sev":"major","kind":"flow","theme":"rmf","what":"Evidence requests, determinations and published results run on a plan that is still 'version 1 · draft'; Add to assessment campaign accepts only campaigns whose plan is a draft.","why":"Assessment precedes an approved assessment plan, against RMF task order.","fix":"Require the plan's approval (SCA, AO concurrence) before requests and determinations; add controls through a plan revision.","evidence":"After publish: 'Plan · Continuous monitoring plan — FY2027 · version 1 · draft' beside 'Continuous monitoring FY2027 results — first set · Published Nov 17'.","where":"campaign-conmon","links":[{"t":"route","r":"campaign-conmon","label":"Continuous monitoring FY2027 campaign"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B20","lane":"B","sev":"major","kind":"flow","theme":"rmf","what":"Ingrid, the program's security engineer, records the SCA's determinations (choosing the assessor's name) and publishes both result sets; they read 'Published … by D. Okafor'. Nothing says it is recorded on the assessor's behalf.","why":"SCA independence: the program team can author and publish the SAR.","fix":"Only the lead assessor publishes; others draft. Say 'recorded as D. Okafor' as risk acceptance does.","evidence":"Record determination: 'Assessor: Nadia Fournier · D. Okafor'. Results: 'Published Nov 17 by D. Okafor'.","where":"campaign-conmon, campaign, dialog: v2k-publish","links":[{"t":"dialog","label":"Publish assessment results"},{"t":"route","r":"campaign-conmon","label":"Continuous monitoring FY2027 campaign"},{"t":"route","r":"campaign","label":"Expanded Control Set Assessment"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B21","lane":"B","sev":"major","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"rmf","what":"Publishing the expanded interim results (1 other than satisfied, 4 partially) opens no operational issue; publishing FY2027 results opens one per determination short of satisfied. IA-2(2) turns Other than satisfied with no issue or POA&M.","why":"Weaknesses from one campaign never reach the POA&M.","fix":"One publish rule: each determination short of satisfied opens an operational issue, whichever campaign.","evidence":"Expanded publish toast mentions no issue; Findings unchanged (44); IA-2(2) 'Other than satisfied · Open assessment findings'. FY2027 publish: '1 operational issue opened'.","where":"assessments, findings","links":[{"t":"route","r":"assessments","label":"Assessments"},{"t":"route","r":"findings","label":"Findings"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B22","lane":"B","sev":"major","kind":"flow","theme":"rmf","what":"A risk created on an issue its POA&M item remediates gets Response 'Accept, if the AO agrees' (the dialog never asks) and 'Request acceptance' as its primary. A risk can only be created after the POA&M item.","why":"Response says accept while a POA&M mitigates; risk assessment follows the remediation it should inform.","fix":"Ask the response (Mitigate, Accept, Transfer) when creating; default Mitigate when a POA&M item answers it; allow the risk before the POA&M.","evidence":"Issue: 'A risk rests on the issue once its POA&M item exists'. Risk page: Rests on the POA&M item; 'Response: Accept, if the AO agrees'.","where":"rec--a-risk-risk--v2k-risk-1, dialog: Create risk","links":[{"t":"dialog","label":"Create risk"},{"t":"route","r":"risks","label":"Risks"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B23","lane":"B","sev":"major","kind":"missing","theme":"rmf","what":"No place records the SCA's risk recommendation: it exists only as the criterion text 'SAR delivered with risk recommendation to the AO'. The ATO step's decision offers Approve / with conditions / Not approved, not ATO, IATT or DATO.","why":"The AO decides without the assessor's recorded recommendation; the decision type is lost.","fix":"Add the SCA recommendation to the SAR step and package; make the ATO decision types ATO, ATO with conditions, IATT, DATO.","evidence":"Registry search for 'recommend…': only the SAR criterion and settings text. Record decision on lifecycle-ato-2: Approve, Approve with conditions, Not approved.","where":"lifecycle-sar-2, authorization","links":[{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-sar-2","label":"Lifecycle › Final assessment and SAR · Increment 2"},{"t":"route","r":"authorization","label":"Authorization"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B24","lane":"B","sev":"major","kind":"flow","theme":"order","what":"Adversarial cybersecurity DT&E (Apr 12 – May 7, 2027) and the SA-24 resiliency exercise (from May 2) are scheduled before TRR (Apr 27) and the IATT (May 18) that authorizes the test configuration.","why":"Adversarial testing on a range would start without test readiness or interim authority.","fix":"Schedule ACD and the exercise after the IATT, or show the IATT as their prerequisite and warn.","evidence":"#cyber-te timeline: '4 · ACD · Apr 12 – May 7, 2027', 'Exercise · May 2 – Jun 1, 2027'. Lifecycle: TRR Apr 27, IATT May 18, 2027.","where":"cyber-te","links":[{"t":"route","r":"cyber-te","label":"Cyber T&E"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B25","lane":"B","sev":"major","kind":"dead-end","theme":"wiring","what":"Cyber T&E's 'Plan the test' answers 'Not saved: Plan a cyber test isn't wired in this prototype'. The same CVI can be planned from Assessments' 'Plan an assessment'.","why":"The page that owns cyber test planning cannot plan one.","fix":"Wire the dialog to the same command Assessments uses, or point to it.","evidence":"#cyber-te → Plan the test → Plan cyber test → toast 'Not saved: Plan a cyber test isn't wired in this prototype'.","where":"cyber-te, dialog: Plan a cyber test","links":[{"t":"dialog","label":"Plan a cyber test"},{"t":"route","r":"cyber-te","label":"Cyber T&E"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B26","lane":"B","sev":"minor","kind":"dead-end","theme":"wiring","what":"Deliverable 'Requirements · 14 controls with no requirement' opens the unfiltered Requirements register (640 requirements), not the 14 controls it counts.","why":"The user must hunt for the 14 controls PDR waits on.","fix":"Link to Controls filtered to No requirement (14).","evidence":"'Not ready: Requirements' → #requirements, All 640; Controls has no No requirement quick view.","where":"lifecycle-pdr-2 → requirements","links":[{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-pdr-2","label":"Lifecycle › PDR · Preliminary design review · Increment 2"},{"t":"route","r":"requirements","label":"Requirements"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B27","lane":"B","sev":"minor","kind":"flow","theme":"rmf","what":"'Develop the SSP' is decided by the Lead assessor (SCA), and 'Select security controls' is 'approved by the SCA'. In RMF the AO (or AODR) approves the plan and baseline; the SCA assesses against them.","why":"The assessor approves what they later assess.","fix":"Make the AO or AODR the decider; keep the SCA as a reviewer.","evidence":"#lifecycle-ssp-2: STEP 2 D. Okafor Lead assessor (SCA), Decides D. Okafor. #lifecycle-sel-2: 'Tailored baseline approved by the SCA'.","where":"lifecycle-ssp-2, lifecycle-sel-2","links":[{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-ssp-2","label":"Lifecycle › Develop the SSP · Increment 2"},{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-sel-2","label":"Lifecycle › Select security controls · Increment 2"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B28","lane":"B","sev":"minor","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"dup","what":"SVR's deliverable names Wes Duarte as owner of 'Cyber T&E · CVI FY2027'; Cyber T&E and Assessments name Ingrid Solberg as the CVI's lead and owner.","why":"Two owners for one test.","fix":"Read the deliverable's owner from the campaign.","evidence":"#lifecycle-svr-2: 'Cyber T&E · CVI FY2027 · Planned Jan 11 · Wes Duarte'. #cyber-te: CVI lead 'Ingrid Solberg'.","where":"lifecycle-svr-2, cyber-te","links":[{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-svr-2","label":"Lifecycle › SVR · System verification review · Increment 2"},{"t":"route","r":"cyber-te","label":"Cyber T&E"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B29","lane":"B","sev":"minor","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"decisions","what":"SSP 3 submission is blocked: 'The categorization has no rationale', while Increment 2's Categorize step is Completed with ITCSC version 3 signed Sep 2.","why":"A signed categorization does not reach the SSP that needs it.","fix":"Fill the SSP's rationale from the signed ITCSC.","evidence":"#ssp-review Readiness: '1 item blocks submission · The categorization has no rationale'. #lifecycle-cat-2: 'ITCSC · Version 3, signed Sep 2'.","where":"ssp-review, lifecycle-cat-2","links":[{"t":"route","r":"ssp-review","label":"SSP 3 · Submit for review"},{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-cat-2","label":"Lifecycle › Categorize the system · Increment 2"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"B30","lane":"B","sev":"minor","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"decisions","what":"Security engineering calls Milestone B, TRR and SVR 'Planned' where Lifecycle says Not started, and its footnote says PDR and CDR 'record no gate criteria yet'. My work's 'Waiting on others' omits a decision the user requested.","why":"Status words differ by page; the requester loses track.","fix":"Use Lifecycle's status words; drop the stale footnote; list requested decisions under Waiting on others.","evidence":"#sse tiles: Milestone B Planned, CDR Not started. After Request decision on the strategy: #my-work Waiting on others lists 2 items, not it.","where":"sse, my-work","links":[{"t":"route","r":"sse","label":"Security engineering"},{"t":"route","r":"my-work","label":"My work"}],"same":["C01"],"lead":null},{"id":"C01","lane":"C","sev":"blocker","kind":"duplication","theme":"decisions","what":"Two sources of truth for gates. After approving PDR on Lifecycle, it reads criteria 4 of 4 met, Requirements 'Traced', Boundary 'Reviewed by the SCA'; Security engineering reads the same PDR 2 of 4; Overview still No requirement 14.","why":"An approval fabricates readiness the records deny, and the ISSM and AO see two different outcomes for one gate.","fix":"Lifecycle owns each gate's criteria, deliverables and decision; Security engineering reads them. Approval records conditions and never flips a deliverable to Ready. One status vocabulary (SSE 'Planned', Lifecycle 'Not started').","evidence":"Reset; #lifecycle-pdr-2 › Record decision › Approve › Record decision. Toast 'PDR approved'. Lifecycle 'Criteria 4 of 4 met … Ready: Requirements Traced … Ready: Boundary Reviewed by the SCA'. #sse 'PDR … Decided Nov 17, 2026 · 2 of 4 met', AR.7 Partly met, SR.6 Not assessed. #overview 'No requirement 14'. Before: both read 2 of 4. Review queue, Overview stage, Home, Programs and My work did follow (148→147, next RMF strategy Dec 15).","where":"#lifecycle-pdr-2 dialog: v2g-decide; #sse; #overview","links":[{"t":"dialog","label":"Record decision"},{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-pdr-2","label":"Lifecycle › PDR · Preliminary design review · Increment 2"},{"t":"route","r":"sse","label":"Security engineering"},{"t":"route","r":"overview","label":"Overview"}],"same":["A15","B02","B13","B30"],"lead":null},{"id":"C02","lane":"C","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"dup","what":"One setup checklist, three values on screen: the page reads 3 of 12 done · 25%, the menu badge beside it reads 20%, the Overview card reads Set up WS-X90 · 2 of 10 steps done.","why":"Nobody can tell how far setup is; each number implies a different list of steps.","fix":"Derive the page header, the badge and the Overview card from one checklist object and show one fraction everywhere.","evidence":"Census at reset: #getting-started '3 of 12 done · 25%' with menu 'Getting started 20%' on the same screen (s02); #overview 'Set up WS-X90 · 2 of 10 steps done' (s03). Counting the page's own items gives 3 of 11.","where":"#getting-started; program menu badge; #overview","links":[{"t":"route","r":"getting-started","label":"Getting started"},{"t":"route","r":"overview","label":"Overview"}],"same":[],"lead":{"verdict":"held","note":"Getting started reads 3 of 12 done · 25%, its menu badge 20%, and Overview's card 2 of 10 steps done."}},{"id":"C03","lane":"C","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"dup","what":"Control status snapshots disagree: the Nov 17 row reads 227 of 560, its preview and page read 176; Nov 13–14 rows read 174 and Nov 15–17 read 227 (+53); Programs says +2 controls since Nov 13.","why":"An immutable audit entry shows two results, and the portfolio trend contradicts the log by 51 controls.","fix":"Take every snapshot, row, preview and change the same way (inherited controls included) and read the trend from those rows.","evidence":"#event-log row 'Nov 17, 23:55 … Snapshot taken … 227 of 560'; clicked it: preview and #rec--v7o-event--0 'Result 176 of 560 controls satisfied' (s04). Rows Nov 13 and Nov 14 '174 of 560'. #portfolio WS-X90 'Since Nov 13 +2 controls' (176−174, own counts) beside '227 of 560'.","where":"#event-log preview: v7o-event 0; #portfolio","links":[{"t":"panel","k":"v7o-event","id":"0","label":"Event preview: Snapshot taken"},{"t":"route","r":"event-log","label":"Settings › Event log"},{"t":"route","r":"portfolio","label":"Programs"}],"same":[],"lead":{"verdict":"held","note":"The Event log's latest snapshot row reads 227 of 560 controls satisfied; its preview reads 176 of 560."}},{"id":"C04","lane":"C","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"dup","what":"Overview's tile says Your tasks 6, assigned to you; its link opens My work, whose Assigned to me view lists 3 items (CVE remediation, Requirements PDR deliverable, configuration baseline audit). The All view has 13.","why":"The number on the program's front page matches no list the user can open.","fix":"Count the tile from My work's Assigned to me rows and open that view, not All.","evidence":"#overview 'Your tasks · assigned to you · 6' → href #my-work. #my-work › Assigned to me: Urgent 1, Due for PDR 1, Coming soon 1. Rail My work 13.","where":"#overview; #my-work","links":[{"t":"route","r":"overview","label":"Overview"},{"t":"route","r":"my-work","label":"My work"}],"same":[],"lead":{"verdict":"held","note":"Overview says \"Your tasks · assigned to you · 6\"; My work's Assigned to me lists 3."}},{"id":"C05","lane":"C","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"decisions","what":"Increment 1's IATT has two dates: Lifecycle says the IATT memo was signed Nov 18, 2025; Authorization's decision history lists an IATT for the developmental test article on Jun 2, 2026, ATD Aug 31, 2026.","why":"The AO's authorization history and the life cycle disagree about when testing was authorized.","fix":"Read the decision history's IATT row from the Lifecycle IATT step (and list Increment 2's planned May 18, 2027 IATT there too).","evidence":"#lifecycle-iatt-1 'IATT · Interim authority to test · Completed · Ready: IATT memo · Signed Nov 18, 2025'. #authorization Decision history 'IATT · Developmental test article · Jun 2, 2026 · Jun 2, 2026 · Aug 31, 2026 · R. Calloway'. Increment 2 IATT May 18, 2027 agrees on Boundary and Lifecycle.","where":"#lifecycle-iatt-1; #authorization","links":[{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle-iatt-1","label":"Lifecycle › IATT · Interim authority to test · Increment 1"},{"t":"route","r":"authorization","label":"Authorization"}],"same":["B06"],"lead":null},{"id":"C06","lane":"C","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"dup","what":"The SCTM workbook's sheets count Requirements 117, Evidence 89, Findings 112; the registers count 640 requirements, 368 evidence artifacts, 44 operational issues and 313 assessment findings. Lifecycle lists the SCTM as a 'Current' PDR deliverable.","why":"The traceability matrix sent to PDR reads a fraction of the program's records under the same names.","fix":"Build the sheets from the full registers, or name them as subsets ('Requirements behind 92 controls'); keep Operational issues and Assessment findings apart.","evidence":"#sctm footer 'SCTM 560 · Controls 560 · Requirements 117 · Evidence 89 · Findings 112 · Risks 40'; note 'The snapshot names the requirements of 92 controls'. Findings sheet mixes rows of Kind 'Operational issue' with determinations. #lifecycle-pdr-2 'Ready: SCTM workbook · Current'.","where":"#sctm sheet tabs; #requirements; #evidence; #findings","links":[{"t":"route","r":"sctm","label":"SCTM workbook"},{"t":"route","r":"requirements","label":"Requirements"},{"t":"route","r":"evidence","label":"Evidence"},{"t":"route","r":"findings","label":"Findings"}],"same":[],"lead":{"verdict":"held","note":"The SCTM workbook's sheet tabs read Requirements 117, Evidence 89, Findings 112; the registers hold 640 requirements and 368 evidence artifacts."}},{"id":"C07","lane":"C","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"dup","what":"Mapping REQ-641 to SA-24 moves Overview, Controls, Lifecycle, My work and the SCTM (14→13 with no requirement) but Baseline still reads No requirement 14, Cyber resiliency '0 of its 10 objectives mapped', Posture '30 mapped nowhere', Requirements 640.","why":"After one edit the Baseline and Overview contradict each other; the analysis pages report a gap already closed.","fix":"Have Baseline's status strip, Cyber resiliency, Posture, Requirements and Traceability read the same control-status and mapping store the Overview reads.","evidence":"Reset; #controls › SA-24 preview › Map a requirement › REQ-641 › Map a requirement. Toast 'REQ-641 maps SA-24: 10 of 10 objectives mapped'. After: #overview 'No requirement 13', #baseline 'No requirement 14', #resiliency 'SA-24 … has 0 of its 10 objectives mapped', #posture '1,761 of 1,791 … 30 are mapped nowhere', #requirements 'Requirements 640', #traceability 'Every requirement maps one'; SCTM Requirements 117→118.","where":"#controls preview: a-tests-control SA-24 dialog: Map a requirement; #baseline; #resiliency; #posture; #requirements; #traceability","links":[{"t":"panel","k":"a-tests-control","id":"SA-24","label":"Control preview: SA-24 Design For Cyber Resiliency"},{"t":"dialog","label":"Map a requirement"},{"t":"route","r":"controls","label":"Controls"},{"t":"route","r":"baseline","label":"Baseline"},{"t":"route","r":"resiliency","label":"Cyber resiliency"},{"t":"route","r":"posture","label":"Posture"},{"t":"route","r":"requirements","label":"Requirements"},{"t":"route","r":"traceability","label":"Traceability"}],"same":["B03"],"lead":null},{"id":"C08","lane":"C","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"dup","what":"Accepting one evidence version moves Evidence (Pending review 87), the Review queue (147) and My work's reviewer row (87), but Overview says 88 waiting on review, the assessor's tracker Ready 88 · Accepted 226, and the Event log adds nothing.","why":"Three screens disagree on the review backlog, and an audit log that claims every review misses one.","fix":"Count Overview's tile, the request tracker and My work's assessor item from the evidence review states; write each review to the Event log.","evidence":"Reset; #evidence-page-e1 › Accept › Save review. Toast 'Accepted: Time source comparison test report…'. After: #evidence 'Pending review 87'; rail Review 147; #my-work '87 evidence versions wait on a reviewer' but '88 requests ready for the assessor'; #overview '88 waiting on review'; #assessments 'Ready 88 · Accepted 226'; #event-log 'Evidence reviews 280' unchanged.","where":"#evidence-page-e1 dialog: Review evidence; #overview; #assessments; #event-log","links":[{"t":"dialog","label":"Review evidence"},{"t":"route","r":"evidence-page-e1","label":"Time source comparison test report"},{"t":"route","r":"overview","label":"Overview"},{"t":"route","r":"assessments","label":"Assessments"},{"t":"route","r":"event-log","label":"Settings › Event log"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"C09","lane":"C","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"dup","what":"Joel Barrantes's page says he owns 19 records in WS-X90: Risks 2, Evidence 0, Checks 0, Open tasks 2 (and 3 further down). Risks says all 40 have no owner; Evidence and Checks list him as owner of several rows.","why":"The person page an ISSM uses for hand-over contradicts every register it summarizes.","fix":"Compute the person page's counts from the registers' owner fields; make the total the sum of the shown categories.","evidence":"#person-joel-barrantes 'Records they own in WS-X90 19 · Evidence 0 · Operational issues 0 · POA&M items 0 · Risks 2 · Open tasks 2 · Checks 0', section 'Open tasks 3'. #risks 'No owner 40'. #evidence rows 'Maintenance session teardown…' and 'Pinned toolchain record export…' owner JB. #checks: Joel owns 'Vulnerability scans run at RA-5's frequency' and 'No open STIG CAT I'.","where":"#person-joel-barrantes; #risks; #evidence; #checks","links":[{"t":"route","r":"person-joel-barrantes","label":"Joel Barrantes"},{"t":"route","r":"risks","label":"Risks"},{"t":"route","r":"evidence","label":"Evidence"},{"t":"route","r":"checks","label":"Checks"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"C10","lane":"C","sev":"blocker","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"dup","what":"Evidence sources says the switch STIG source was never imported (Queued); STIG checklists shows two switch checklists imported Aug 18. Integrations counts 2 STIG Viewer checklists; STIG checklists lists 4. Checks says no STIG data is loaded.","why":"The engineer cannot tell whether the switch was ever checked, which decides CM-6 and the CAT findings.","fix":"Draw Integrations' counts and Checks' footnote from Evidence sources, and Evidence sources' import history from the checklists it produced.","evidence":"#sources 'DISA STIG checklist — internal Ethernet switch · Never imported · Every 90 days · Queued'; #event-log 'Nov 13, 20:22 Joel Barrantes Import queued DISA STIG checklist — internal Ethernet switch'. #stigs 'Internal Ethernet Switch · Cisco IOS Switch NDM V3R6 · STIG Viewer 2.18 · Aug 18 · Priya Raghavan' and 'L2S V3R1 · Aug 18'. #integrations 'STIG Viewer checklists … WS-X90: 2 checklists'. #checks footnote 'no ACAS or STIG data is loaded'.","where":"#sources; #stigs; #integrations; #checks","links":[{"t":"route","r":"sources","label":"Evidence sources"},{"t":"route","r":"stigs","label":"STIG checklists"},{"t":"route","r":"integrations","label":"Library › Integrations"},{"t":"route","r":"checks","label":"Checks"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"C11","lane":"C","sev":"blocker","kind":"duplication","theme":"dup","what":"Recurring checks live on four pages with different cadences and states: the ACAS scan is monthly and In progress (ConMon, Schedule), every 7 days and 31 days past (Evidence sources), Overdue (Checks). Checks counts Overdue 4, ConMon 2.","why":"The ISSO and the AO's conditions read different overdue counts for the same monitoring plan.","fix":"Continuous monitoring owns each recurring check; Checks merges into it, Schedule shows its runs as tasks, Evidence sources reads the import cadence from it.","evidence":"#conmon 'ACAS vulnerability scan, mission network · Monthly · Oct 11 · Nov 15 · 2 days ago · In progress'; 'STIG compliance scan · Monthly · Nov 11 · Blocked'. #schedule same rows. #sources 'ACAS … Oct 10 · 31d past cadence · Every 7 days'; 'DISA STIG checklist — mission computing (RHEL 9) · Every 90 days · Current'. #stigs RHEL 9 'Next import Due Jan 11, 2027'. #checks 'Needs attention 5 · Overdue 4', RA-5 scan 'Overdue Nov 15'; #conmon 'Overdue 2'.","where":"#checks; #conmon; #schedule; #sources","links":[{"t":"route","r":"checks","label":"Checks"},{"t":"route","r":"conmon","label":"Continuous monitoring"},{"t":"route","r":"schedule","label":"Schedule"},{"t":"route","r":"sources","label":"Evidence sources"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"C12","lane":"C","sev":"blocker","kind":"dead-end","theme":"wiring","what":"Mission Computer version 2 (the fix for the 8-days-late CVE) is a banner on Home ('Open offer'), Composition and Inheritance ('Review version 2', two differently worded Take version dialogs); Take version 2 answers 'Not saved … isn't wired'.","why":"My work's most urgent item has three entry points and none completes; nothing moves (4 behind, version 1 in use).","fix":"One call to action, on Inheritance (or Composition), opening one Take version dialog that is wired and updates Components, Inventory, Supplier, POA&M and Checks.","evidence":"Reset; #composition › Review version 2 › Take version 2 → toast 'Not saved: Take version 2 of Mission Computer isn't wired in this prototype'. #inheritance › Review version 2 opens a dialog with a different first paragraph. #home › Open offer → #component-mc-findings Offer preview. After: #components '4 behind', Inventory AST-109001 'version 1', POA&M CVE item 'Not started', #checks 'No known-affected component in use … Overdue'.","where":"#home, #composition, #inheritance dialog: Take version 2 of Mission Computer","links":[{"t":"dialog","label":"Take version 2 of Mission Computer"},{"t":"route","r":"home","label":"Home"},{"t":"route","r":"composition","label":"Composition"},{"t":"route","r":"inheritance","label":"Inheritance"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"C13","lane":"C","sev":"blocker","kind":"dead-end","theme":"wiring","what":"In the Findings–POA&M–Risks–Threats set, four of five verbs I tried answer 'Not saved … isn't wired': Assign owner, Deactivate finding, Change planned date, Link ATT&CK technique. Only Request acceptance works.","why":"'Give an owner to 40 open risks' is asked by Overview, My work, Getting started and the Monday digest and cannot be done.","fix":"Wire Assign owner first (risks, issues, POA&M items) and have Overview, My work, Notifications and People recount owners from it.","evidence":"Reset; #risks › first row checkbox › Assign owner › Priya Raghavan › Assign owner → 'Not saved: Assign owner isn't wired in this prototype'; counts stay 'No owner 40' on #risks, #overview, #my-work, #notifications. Same answer for Deactivate (#findings REQ-100), Change planned date (#poam REQ-100), Link technique (#threats).","where":"#risks dialog: Assign owner; #findings dialog: Deactivate finding; #poam dialog: Change planned date; #threats dialog: Link ATT&CK technique","links":[{"t":"dialog","label":"Assign owner"},{"t":"dialog","label":"Deactivate finding"},{"t":"dialog","label":"Change planned date"},{"t":"dialog","label":"Link ATT&CK technique"},{"t":"route","r":"risks","label":"Risks"},{"t":"route","r":"findings","label":"Findings"},{"t":"route","r":"poam","label":"POA&M"},{"t":"route","r":"threats","label":"Threats"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"C14","lane":"C","sev":"major","kind":"duplication","theme":"dup","what":"Five inboxes, no shared count: My work 13 ('Nothing waits on your approval'), Review 148 ('Waiting on me 0'), AI agents 7 ('Waiting on you'), Package room's access request ('Waiting on you'), and a bell '1 unread' holding 2 comments.","why":"The reader is told nothing waits on them in two places and that 8 things do in two others.","fix":"My work is the one personal inbox (assigned, needs my approval incl. AI runs and access requests, waiting on others); Review stays the workspace register; the bell holds mentions only.","evidence":"#my-work › Needs my approval 'Nothing waits on your approval'; #review-queue › Waiting on me 'None does today'; #ai-drafts 'All 7', each card 'Waiting on you'; #package-room 'Access requests 1 › Waiting on you'; bell aria-label 'Inbox, 1 unread', popover 'Comments 2'. Request acceptance on a risk (wired) left Review at 148.","where":"#my-work; #review-queue; #ai-drafts; #package-room; top bar Inbox","links":[{"t":"route","r":"my-work","label":"My work"},{"t":"route","r":"review-queue","label":"Review queue"},{"t":"route","r":"ai-drafts","label":"AI agents"},{"t":"route","r":"package-room","label":"Package room"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"C15","lane":"C","sev":"major","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"dup","what":"The queue counts All 148 and the rail badge 148, but the table lists 21 rows ('1–21 of 148', 25 per page, no next page); only 5 of the 88 evidence versions pending review appear.","why":"The register cannot show most of what its badge counts, so the backlog cannot be worked from it.","fix":"List every counted row with working pages, or count only the rows listed.","evidence":"#review-queue: 21 rows (Gate to decide 8, Evidence to accept 5, Discussion 4, Package 1, Results 1, Product assessment 1, Component offer 1), pager '1–21 of 148 · 25 per page · ‹ ›' with no controls. Accepting one evidence version changed the count to 147, so the count is live and the list is not.","where":"#review-queue","links":[{"t":"route","r":"review-queue","label":"Review queue"}],"same":[],"lead":{"verdict":"held","note":"The Review queue reads All 148 and \"1–21 of 148\": 21 rows drawn and no next page."}},{"id":"C16","lane":"C","sev":"major","kind":"duplication","theme":"dup","what":"Inheritance counts 130 controls from 5 sources (components included); Host & providers, Overview and Controls count 76 (52 inherited). A provider added on Host & providers reaches Settings and Overview but not Inheritance or Boundary. Three different add-provider dialogs.","why":"'Inherited' means two numbers, and the boundary drawing misses a provider the program now inherits from.","fix":"Merge Inheritance into Host & providers (providers and library components, one count, one Add); Boundary and Authorization read it; Settings keeps the workspace catalog only.","evidence":"Reset; #hosts › Add provider › Integration laboratory hosting enclave → toast '… added: 3 controls inherited'. After: #hosts 'Providers 4 · 79 · Inherited 55', #overview '55 inherited', #common-controls 'WS-X90 Sentinel Mission System: 3 inherited'; #inheritance 'Elements 5 Controls 130 Sources 5' and #boundary 'What it covers 17' unchanged. Dialogs: 'Add provider' (hosts), 'Add provider' (settings, different fields), 'Add common control provider' (inheritance). Taking PE-13 back did reach all pages.","where":"#hosts; #inheritance; #common-controls; #boundary; #interconnections","links":[{"t":"route","r":"hosts","label":"Host & providers"},{"t":"route","r":"inheritance","label":"Inheritance"},{"t":"route","r":"common-controls","label":"Settings › Host systems & providers"},{"t":"route","r":"boundary","label":"Boundary"},{"t":"route","r":"interconnections","label":"Interconnections"}],"same":[],"lead":{"verdict":"held","note":"Host & providers counts 76 controls from providers (52 inherited, 24 hybrid); Inheritance counts 130 controls from 5 sources."}},{"id":"C17","lane":"C","sev":"major","kind":"duplication","theme":"dup","what":"Evidence sources (program) and Integrations (Library) carry the same tabs (Available 11, Connected 7, Errors 1) that jump between program menu and rail. Import file on the ACAS source opens a 6-step Add source wizard ending 'Not saved'.","why":"The user changes area by clicking a tab, and cannot import a new scan into an existing source.","fix":"Integrations lists connectors only; Evidence sources (or an Evidence › Sources tab) owns a program's sources and imports; Import file imports a file into that source.","evidence":"#sources tabs 'Available 11' → #integrations, #integrations 'Connected 7' → #sources. #sources › ACAS row › Import file → 'Add source' Type, System, Hosts, Scope, Threshold, Review › Import → 'Not saved: Add source isn't wired in this prototype'. Banner names 'Container image scan — telemetry services · rejected Oct 30', a source the 7-row register does not list.","where":"#sources; #integrations","links":[{"t":"route","r":"sources","label":"Evidence sources"},{"t":"route","r":"integrations","label":"Library › Integrations"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"C18","lane":"C","sev":"major","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"wiring","what":"Map a requirement offers REQ-641–643 as existing requirements before the Requirement drafter's run is approved; after Approve all ('applied under your name') they are still absent from Requirements (640) and Traceability.","why":"Unapproved AI drafts act as requirements in one place and approved ones vanish in another.","fix":"Offer only requirements in the register; an approved draft joins the register (641, 642, 643) and Traceability at once.","evidence":"Reset; SA-24 › Map a requirement: options 'REQ-641 · Mission functions continue…', 'REQ-642', 'REQ-643'. #requirements search '641' finds nothing. #ai-drafts › Requirement drafter › Approve all → toast '3 requirements approved: they are applied under your name'; #requirements still 'Requirements 640', no REQ-641; Needs approval 7→6.","where":"#controls dialog: Map a requirement; #ai-drafts; #requirements","links":[{"t":"dialog","label":"Map a requirement"},{"t":"route","r":"controls","label":"Controls"},{"t":"route","r":"ai-drafts","label":"AI agents"},{"t":"route","r":"requirements","label":"Requirements"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"C19","lane":"C","sev":"major","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"wiring","what":"People omits Marcus Ryde, whom the PDR decision waits on and who co-edits SSP 3. Ingrid Solberg is 'No RMF role' on People, Security engineer on Overview, ISSE on ITCSC. Marcus is Chief engineer, Engineer and Component owner.","why":"The roster cannot answer who decides the next gate or what the reader's own role is.","fix":"One people-and-roles record per program read by People, Overview Team, ITCSC §11, SSP access and Permissions; include gate deciders.","evidence":"#people lists 11 (no Marcus Ryde); #review-queue PDR 'Waiting on MR Marcus Ryde'; #ssps 'Editing now Priya Raghavan, Marcus Ryde'. #people 'Ingrid Solberg · No RMF role'; #overview 'Security engineer · Ingrid Solberg (You)'; #itcsc 'Director of engineering / ISSE · Ingrid Solberg'. Marcus: #sse 'Chief engineer', Assign owner 'Engineer', #ssps 'Component owner'. 'Local developer' is an Assessor (SCA); AO and system owner share the RC avatar.","where":"#people; #overview Team; #itcsc §11; #ssps preview; #permissions","links":[{"t":"route","r":"people","label":"People"},{"t":"route","r":"overview","label":"Overview"},{"t":"route","r":"itcsc","label":"ITCSC"},{"t":"route","r":"ssps","label":"Plans"},{"t":"route","r":"permissions","label":"Settings › Roles & permissions"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"C20","lane":"C","sev":"major","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"dup","what":"AC-1 reads Partially satisfied, Determined by Program assessment, 17 of 17 assessed, and in the same preview 'No assessment has judged AC-1 yet'; its page shows Assessment 0 and Findings 0. AU-7 reads System-specific with Next step 'Inherited'.","why":"A determination with no assessment behind it undermines every status count the Overview shows.","fix":"Show the finding that determined the status and its campaign; put component inheritance in the Responsibility column.","evidence":"#controls › AC-1 preview 'Status Partially satisfied · 17 of 17 mapped · 17 with evidence · 17 assessed · Determined by Program assessment … Findings and risks 0 · No assessment has judged AC-1 yet'. Page tabs 'Assessment 0 · Findings 0'. #controls AU-7 row 'Satisfied · System-specific · 4 of 4 · Inherited'; #inheritance lists AU-7 under Audit Log Collector.","where":"#controls preview: a-tests-control AC-1; #rec--a-tests-control--AC-1","links":[{"t":"route","r":"rec--a-tests-control--AC-1","label":"AC-1 control page"},{"t":"panel","k":"a-tests-control","id":"AC-1","label":"Control preview: AC-1 Policy and Procedures"},{"t":"route","r":"controls","label":"Controls"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"C21","lane":"C","sev":"major","kind":"duplication","theme":"dup","what":"Both pages carry package version 2's readiness, worded differently (SSP 3 approved vs published); Package room's 'Version 2: items ready' jumps to Authorization, its 'Open version 2' stays put, and Share the package is not wired.","why":"Two pages own one package; the readiness rule differs by page.","fix":"Authorization owns versions, contents, readiness and decision; Package room becomes its Sharing tab (recipients, access requests, access log).","evidence":"#authorization Submit dialog 'SSP 3 approved · Increment 2 results published · POA&M current' (Submit disabled). #package-room-versions 'POA&M current Done · SSP 3 published Draft today · Increment 2 results published'. #package-room 'Version 2: items ready to submit 1 of 3 ›' → #authorization; 'Open version 2' → #package-room-versions; #overview 'Open package' → #authorization; Share → 'Not saved: Share the package isn't wired'.","where":"#authorization; #package-room","links":[{"t":"route","r":"authorization","label":"Authorization"},{"t":"route","r":"package-room","label":"Package room"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"C22","lane":"C","sev":"major","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"wiring","what":"'Customer A' names another program (X800 Rail Integration), yet WS-X90's baseline applies a 'Customer A Tailoring' layer (−4 controls) and Cyber T&E counts 'Customer A's requirements document, 14 requirements' as WS-X90's input.","why":"An AO reading WS-X90's baseline sees another program's tailoring in it.","fix":"Rename the layer and the document for WS-X90's own customer, or explain the relationship; keep 'Customer A' for the X800 program only.","evidence":"#baseline stack row 4 'Customer A Tailoring v1 · Overlay · −4 · 546'; #itcsc 'Customer A Tailoring · −4 · 546 · Not on the ITCSC: a customer's tailoring'; #cyber-te Phase 1 'Customer A's requirements document, 14 requirements'; #portfolio 'Customer A · X800 Rail Integration' (Air Defense).","where":"#baseline; #itcsc §6; #cyber-te preview: v7a-phase 1; #portfolio","links":[{"t":"panel","k":"v7a-phase","id":"1","label":"Phase preview: Phase 1 · Understand cybersecurity requirements"},{"t":"route","r":"baseline","label":"Baseline"},{"t":"route","r":"itcsc","label":"ITCSC"},{"t":"route","r":"cyber-te","label":"Cyber T&E"},{"t":"route","r":"portfolio","label":"Programs"}],"same":[],"lead":{"verdict":"held","note":"WS-X90's baseline stack has \"Customer A Tailoring v1 · Overlay · +0 −4 · 546\"."}},{"id":"C23","lane":"C","sev":"major","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"wiring","what":"WS-X90 inherits 15 hybrid controls from the Corporate identity provider (AC-2 reads Satisfied through it), which is Not authorized, and whose own program row reads past due at TMRR with 0 of 287 controls satisfied.","why":"An SCA or AO would refuse inheritance from an unauthorized provider; the screens never connect the two facts.","fix":"Flag a provider without an authorization on Host & providers and on each control that leans on it; link the provider to its program row.","evidence":"#hosts 'Corporate identity provider · Enterprise service · 15 · 0 · 15 · 0 · Not authorized'. #controls 'AC-2 · Satisfied · Hybrid · Corporate identity provider'. #portfolio 'Corporate identity provider · Past due: TMRR · next RMF strategy Aug 21, 2025 · 0 of 287'. #interconnections 'Corporate identity provider (PRG-1013)'.","where":"#hosts; #controls; #portfolio","links":[{"t":"route","r":"hosts","label":"Host & providers"},{"t":"route","r":"controls","label":"Controls"},{"t":"route","r":"portfolio","label":"Programs"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"C24","lane":"C","sev":"major","kind":"flow","theme":"order","what":"Getting started sits only in the program menu but its first step is workspace setup (catalog, roles, deadlines, notifications). 'Adopt the 12 proposed deadlines' opens Deadlines, which has no adopt action; Edit deadlines edits only the high finding deadline.","why":"A workspace task is repeated per program and its step cannot be completed where it sends the user.","fix":"Workspace steps go to Settings (or Home) once; the program keeps an Overview setup card. Give Deadlines an 'Adopt proposed' action that ticks the step.","evidence":"#getting-started 'Set up the workspace, give records owners, then close WS-X90's gaps'; rail has no Getting started. 'Go to deadlines' → #deadlines: only 'Edit deadlines' → dialog 'Edit high finding deadline'; Save deadline gives no confirmation; page and badge unchanged (3 of 12, 20%).","where":"#getting-started; #deadlines","links":[{"t":"route","r":"getting-started","label":"Getting started"},{"t":"route","r":"deadlines","label":"Settings › Deadlines"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"C25","lane":"C","sev":"major","kind":"flow","theme":"order","what":"The menu groups by artifact type, not by RMF step or acquisition phase: Baseline (Select) follows Inventory, STIG checklists and Evidence sources; gate criteria (Security engineering) and Inheritance hide in collapsed Analysis; People, RMF's first step, sits last.","why":"A team cannot read the build, run and assess order from the menu; related pages sit groups apart.","fix":"Order by RMF step with Lifecycle on top: Prepare, Categorize, Select, Implement, Assess, Authorize, Monitor. Merge seven pages (see C/order.json).","evidence":"Menu: Overview, Lifecycle, Getting started, ITCSC | System: Boundary … Evidence sources | Compliance: Baseline, Controls, Plans, Requirements, SCTM workbook, Evidence, Checks, Policies | Assess | Risk | Analysis (closed): Posture, Cyber resiliency, Security engineering, Traceability, Inheritance | Authorize | Monitor | People. Proposal in SP/vanta/review/C/order.json.","where":"program menu (core.js PROGRAM)","links":[{"t":"route","r":"overview","label":"The program menu"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"C26","lane":"C","sev":"minor","kind":"duplication","theme":"dup","what":"Facts repeated on one page: Findings shows the open-issue count six times; Authorization the ATO date and ATD three times each; SSE PDR's due date three times plus the menu; Lifecycle's header and menu both '3 of 5 ready'.","why":"Repetition breaks the budget's 'each fact once' and makes real differences hard to spot.","fix":"Show each fact once per page: drop count cards that repeat tab counts, header facts that repeat Decision in force, and the page's stage line where the menu shows it.","evidence":"#findings 'By issue 44 … 44 open … 44 open … All 44 … 1–12 of 44' + menu 'Findings 44'. #authorization 'Signed Sep 18, 2026 · ATD Sep 17, 2029', 'Decision in force … Sep 18, 2026 … Sep 17, 2029', Decision history 'Sep 18, 2026 · Sep 18, 2026 · Sep 17, 2029'. #sse callout, strip and table each 'Nov 24'. #boundary repeats 'ATO · Sep 18, 2026' on six rows.","where":"#findings; #authorization; #sse; #lifecycle; #overview","links":[{"t":"route","r":"findings","label":"Findings"},{"t":"route","r":"authorization","label":"Authorization"},{"t":"route","r":"sse","label":"Security engineering"},{"t":"route","r":"lifecycle","label":"Lifecycle"},{"t":"route","r":"overview","label":"Overview"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"C27","lane":"C","sev":"minor","kind":"inconsistency","theme":"dup","what":"Count mismatches: Threats 32 techniques vs Cyber T&E 31; STIG triage '23 CAT II matched' on the laptop checklist's 17 open CAT II; root element 'Open issues 43' vs 44; Traceability 'Reach a risk 52, 52 open' beside 40 risks.","why":"Each looks like an error even where the definitions differ.","fix":"Use one count per fact, or label the definition (e.g. '52 requirements reach an open risk').","evidence":"#threats 'Techniques 32 · Enterprise 31 · ICS 1'; #cyber-te '23 risks name 31 ATT&CK techniques'. #ai-drafts 'STIG triage: 23 CAT II open rules … STIG checklist · Maintenance Laptop'; #stigs Maintenance Laptop '1 · 17 · 3'. Element CN-109000 'Open issues 43'; #posture/#findings 44. #traceability 'Reach a risk 52 · 52 open'; #risks 'Register 40'.","where":"#threats; #cyber-te; #ai-drafts; #stigs; #rec--v7p-el--CN-109000; #traceability","links":[{"t":"route","r":"rec--v7p-el--CN-109000","label":"Element CN-109000 page"},{"t":"route","r":"threats","label":"Threats"},{"t":"route","r":"cyber-te","label":"Cyber T&E"},{"t":"route","r":"ai-drafts","label":"AI agents"},{"t":"route","r":"stigs","label":"STIG checklists"},{"t":"route","r":"traceability","label":"Traceability"}],"same":[],"lead":null},{"id":"C28","lane":"C","sev":"minor","kind":"wording","theme":"wiring","what":"Workspace Settings holds WS-X90's own records: the Event log reads 'in WS-X90 since Jun 30', and My account › Notifications digests 'Everything waiting on WS-X90'. With nine programs these read as one program's pages filed as workspace settings.","why":"A program's audit trail is found outside the program's menu.","fix":"Give the program menu an Activity (event log) entry, keep a workspace-wide Event log filterable by program in Settings.","evidence":"#event-log 'Who did what to which record, and when, in WS-X90 since Jun 30'; #notifications digest 'A summary of everything waiting on WS-X90'; rail Settings menu: Deadlines, Notifications, Roles & permissions, Enclaves & markings, Host systems & providers, Event log | My account: Notifications.","where":"rail Settings › Event log, Host systems & providers, Notifications","links":[{"t":"route","r":"event-log","label":"Settings › Event log"},{"t":"route","r":"common-controls","label":"Settings › Host systems & providers"},{"t":"route","r":"notifications","label":"Settings › Notifications"}],"same":[],"lead":null}],"dup":[{"id":"dup-status","job":"Control status","pages":["overview","controls","baseline","posture","resiliency","requirements","traceability","sctm"],"what":"After results are published, Overview and Controls go from 227 to 240 satisfied while Baseline, Posture and Authorization stay at 227. After Map a requirement, Overview goes from 14 to 13 with no requirement and Baseline still says 14.","owner":"One status that every page reads","ids":["B03","B04","C07"]},{"id":"dup-gates","job":"Gates","pages":["lifecycle","sse","schedule","review-queue"],"what":"After Approve, Lifecycle shows PDR at 4 of 4 criteria met and Security engineering shows 2 of 4. RM.3 is met on one gate and Not assessed on Security engineering.","owner":"Lifecycle; Security engineering's outcomes become the gate's criteria","ids":["C01","B13","B30"]},{"id":"dup-providers","job":"Providers","pages":["boundary","hosts","inheritance","common-controls"],"what":"Inheritance counts 130 controls from 5 sources; Host & providers counts 76. There are three different Add provider dialogs, and a provider added on one page doesn't reach the others.","owner":"Host & providers, with Inheritance folded in","ids":["C16","C23"]},{"id":"dup-inbox","job":"What waits on me","pages":["my-work","review-queue","ai-drafts","package-room"],"what":"Five different answers. Review says 148 and lists 21; Overview says \"Your tasks 6\" and My work lists 3.","owner":"My work","ids":["C14","C15","C04"]},{"id":"dup-guide","job":"Getting started","pages":["getting-started","overview"],"what":"3 of 12 (25%) on the page, 20% on its menu badge, 2 of 10 on Overview.","owner":"One checklist; the workspace steps move to Settings","ids":["C02","C24"]},{"id":"dup-checks","job":"Recurring checks","pages":["checks","conmon","schedule","sources"],"what":"The ACAS scan is monthly on two pages and every 7 days on another; the overdue counts are 4 and 2.","owner":"Continuous monitoring","ids":["C11"]},{"id":"dup-imports","job":"Imports","pages":["sources","integrations","stigs"],"what":"The switch STIG source is \"never imported\" on Evidence sources, while STIG checklists shows two switch checklists imported Aug 18.","owner":"Evidence sources","ids":["C10","C17"]},{"id":"dup-auth","job":"Authorization","pages":["authorization","package-room"],"what":"Readiness is worded differently on each (SSP 3 approved, SSP 3 published); the POA&M count is 42 on one and 41 on the other.","owner":"Package room becomes a tab of Authorization","ids":["C21","B05"]},{"id":"dup-sctm","job":"SCTM workbook","pages":["sctm","requirements","evidence","findings"],"what":"The sheets hold 117 requirements, 89 evidence items and 112 findings; the registers hold 640 requirements, 368 evidence artifacts, 44 operational issues and 313 assessment findings. PDR still lists the workbook as Current.","owner":"Build the sheets from the registers","ids":["C06"]}],"menu":{"today":[{"group":null,"closed":false,"pages":["Overview","Lifecycle","Getting started","ITCSC"]},{"group":"System","closed":false,"pages":["Boundary","Host & providers","Composition","Inventory","STIG checklists","Interconnections","Ports & protocols","Evidence sources"]},{"group":"Compliance","closed":false,"pages":["Baseline","Controls","Plans","Requirements","SCTM workbook","Evidence","Checks","Policies"]},{"group":"Assess","closed":false,"pages":["Assessments","Cyber T&E"]},{"group":"Risk","closed":false,"pages":["Findings","POA&M","Risks","Threats"]},{"group":"Analysis","closed":true,"pages":["Posture","Cyber resiliency","Security engineering","Traceability","Inheritance"]},{"group":"Authorize","closed":false,"pages":["Authorization","Package room"]},{"group":"Monitor","closed":true,"pages":["Continuous monitoring","Schedule"]},{"group":null,"closed":false,"pages":["People"]}],"proposed":[{"group":null,"pages":["Overview (stage strip, setup card, team)","Lifecycle (gates and RMF steps of each increment, with each gate's security outcomes)"]},{"group":"Prepare","pages":["People & roles (People + Permissions' RMF roles on the program)","Boundary","Interconnections","Ports & protocols","Composition (Assets tab = Inventory)","Host & providers (absorbs Inheritance: providers and library components, one inherited count)"]},{"group":"Categorize & select","pages":["ITCSC","Baseline","Threats (threat-informed tailoring)","Cyber resiliency"]},{"group":"Implement","pages":["Requirements (Traceability as its chain view)","Controls (SCTM workbook as its spreadsheet view, same counts)","Plans (SSP and CP, IRP, CMP)","Policies","STIG checklists"]},{"group":"Assess","pages":["Assessments","Evidence (Sources tab = Evidence sources)","Cyber T&E","Findings (operational issues and assessment findings)"]},{"group":"Authorize","pages":["POA&M","Risks","Authorization (Sharing tab = Package room)"]},{"group":"Monitor","pages":["Continuous monitoring (absorbs Checks; runs shown as Schedule tasks)","Posture","Activity (the program's event log)"]}],"merges":[{"id":"merge-sse","from":"Security engineering","to":"Lifecycle","why":"A gate's security outcomes are its criteria, so they belong on the gate.","ids":["C01","B13","B30"]},{"id":"merge-inheritance","from":"Inheritance","to":"Host & providers","why":"One page for what the program takes from providers and library components, with one inherited count.","ids":["C16"]},{"id":"merge-package-room","from":"Package room","to":"Authorization","why":"As a Sharing tab: both carry package version 2's readiness today.","ids":["C21"]},{"id":"merge-checks","from":"Checks","to":"Continuous monitoring","why":"Both list the same recurring checks, with different cadences.","ids":["C11"]},{"id":"merge-schedule","from":"Schedule","to":"Continuous monitoring and My work","why":"Its runs go to Continuous monitoring and its personal tasks to My work; the reviews already moved to Lifecycle.","ids":["C11"]},{"id":"merge-sources","from":"Evidence sources","to":"Evidence","why":"As a Sources tab; Integrations keeps the connectors only.","ids":["C17","C10"]},{"id":"merge-traceability","from":"Traceability","to":"Requirements","why":"As the chain view: a requirement's record already holds its chain.","ids":[]},{"id":"merge-inventory","from":"Inventory","to":"Composition","why":"As an Assets tab (optional).","ids":[]}],"moves":[{"id":"move-getting-started","from":"Getting started","to":"Settings or Home","why":"Its workspace steps are done once; the program keeps the setup card on its Overview.","ids":["C24","C02"]},{"id":"move-approvals","from":"AI agents' Needs approval and Package room's access requests","to":"My work › Needs my approval","why":"One place for what waits on the reader.","ids":["C14"]}],"why":["Groups are artifact types, not RMF steps: Baseline (Select) comes after Inventory, STIG checklists and Evidence sources (Implement and Assess inputs).","Gate criteria (Security engineering) and common-control inheritance (Inheritance) sit in a collapsed Analysis group at the end, far from Lifecycle and Host & providers, and duplicate them (C01, C16).","People holds the RMF roles, the first thing DoDI 8510.01's Prepare step records, and sits last.","Evidence sits in Compliance though it is the assessor's input; Checks (Compliance) and Continuous monitoring (Monitor) list the same recurring checks (C11).","Getting started mixes workspace setup with program gaps and lives only in the program menu (C24).","The acquisition phases (TMRR: SRR, SFR, PDR; EMD: CDR, TRR, IATT; Production: ATO, IOC) live only on Lifecycle; the menu gives no sense of which pages serve the current gate."],"tweak":{"id":"menu-evidence","text":"My one change to the proposal: Evidence goes under Implement, next to the requirements that cite it, rather than under Assess."},"result":"36 program-menu entries become 27 in six RMF groups under Overview and Lifecycle."},"fixes":[{"id":"fix-1","title":"One source for each fact","text":"Control status, gate state, authorization decisions, people and roles, and the setup checklist each live in one place, and every page reads it. That clears most of the disagreements.","ids":["B03","B04","B05","C02","C03","C04","C06","C07","C08","C09","C15","C16","C21"]},{"id":"fix-2","title":"Gates record only the decision","text":"Each deliverable's state comes from its own record. Approve waits, or asks for conditions, while items are open, and conditions become tracked items with an owner and a due date.","ids":["A15","B01","B02","B08","B10","B11","B12","B14","C01"]},{"id":"fix-3","title":"A created program becomes a real program","text":"Its pages show what the wizard recorded, every empty page gets a first action, the chain from requirement to package works, and only the switcher changes programs.","ids":["A03","A04","A05","A06","A07","A10","A11","A13","A14"]},{"id":"fix-4","title":"Fold and reorder the menu","text":"Order it by RMF step and fold eight pages into the pages that own their jobs, as Menu order shows.","ids":["C24","C25","C14","C16","C17","C21","C11"]},{"id":"fix-5","title":"Add the missing RMF records","text":"The SCA's recommendation, the AO's decision types (ATO, IATT, DATO), determinations by assessment objective, and plan approval before work starts.","ids":["B18","B19","B20","B23","B27","B06","B09"]}],"dropped":["B07"],"summary":{"date":"Nov 19, 2026","version":"version 15","answer":"The order of the work makes sense, but the system doesn't hold together yet. Lifecycle's 19 steps follow RMF and the acquisition life cycle, the wizard completes, and on WS-X90 you can take a control from a campaign through published results to an operational issue, a POA&M item, a risk and the AO's acceptance. Three things break it.","recheck":"I re-ran 15 of the most serious findings myself: 14 held and 1 didn't (B07, under Dropped). Each re-checked finding says what I saw."}}; })();
